

              --> ELAN Tree Automata Library <--

                           Sept. 98



implements basic algorithms on tree automata, such as: intersection,
union, cleaning and renaming as well as algorithms described in 	

[1] T. Genet Decidable approximations of sets of descendants and sets
    of normal forms. In T. Nipkow, editor, Proceedings 9th
    International Conference on Rewriting Tecniques and Applications, 
    Tsukuba (Japan), volume 1379 of Lecture Notes in Computer Science, 
    pages 151-165. Springer-Verlag, 1998.


This ELAN Library requires ELAN version 3.0 or greater.


The Library can be directly used through three different interfaces:
-------------------------------------------------------------------

1) For basic automata manipulation and computation, use the interface
   "automaton.lgi". An example of specification is also provided:
   "ex_automaton.spc". To run basic operations on this specification
   simply type:

	elan automaton.lgi ex_automaton.spc

   Have a look at the file "ex_automaton.spc" for specification syntax
   and examples of queries.




2) For computing approximation automaton (see [1]) or automaton
   recognising set of irreducible terms, use the interface
   "nf_automaton.lgi". To see an example, try:

	elan nf_automaton.lgi ex_nf_automaton.spc

   Have a look at the file "ex_nf_automaton.spc" for specification
   syntax and examples of queries. 



3) For proving termination of sequential reduction relation (see [1]), 
   use the interface "nf_automaton.lgi".
   module. For example, try:

	elan termination.lgi ex_termination.spc

   Have a look at the file "ex_termination.spc" for specification
   syntax examples of queries.

For a compiled version
elan <file>.lgi <spec_file>.spc ; gmake --file <file>.make ; a.out


*******************************************************************************
*                                                                             *
*   VERY IMPORTANT: Please check that for all rules l->r in your TRSs,        *
*   the set of variables of r is INCLUDED in the set of variables of l, and   *
*   l is a linar term.                                                        *
*                                                                             *
*******************************************************************************





